meta {
  name: Set Primary Household Address (Unknown Address)
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/households/{{householdId}}/addresses/000000000000000000000000/primary
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 404 — not an entry in this household's book", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(404);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /households/:id/addresses/:addressId/primary

  Make an address from the book the household's **primary** — a **swap**, not a
  copy: the entry leaves the book and becomes `propertyAddress`, and the primary
  it replaces joins the book as **"Previous address"**. Each address lives in
  exactly one place.

  - **Module:** `clients` OR `crm_service`
  - **Permission:** `clients:write` **OR** `crm_service:write`
  - **Data scope:** `own` collapses to **branch**

  This request names an id that is in no book, so it exercises the 404 and
  changes nothing; the swap itself is covered by the e2e suite.

  ## Response
  The whole **`HouseholdView`**.

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | Both modules disabled, or the caller holds neither write |
  | 404 | Household outside scope, or `addressId` is not an entry in its book (the primary is not an entry) |
}
